## Target identity

The protected subject is L'Homme rendered as a daylight tailored ginger silhouette: polished bergamot and literal lemon reveal a wet-cut ginger cortex; warm fibrous ginger tissue passes into violet-green cloth with restrained basil and pepper; literal cedar and vetiver carry the subject into a hayed, yielding base; one Romandolide aura extends the dry woody outline.

The pleasure hypothesis is continuity between crisp cut, supple cloth, and dry wood. This control does not optimize for scores and does not claim pleasure. It exists to provide one current-stock family comparator for later blinded flanker work.

Excluded takeovers remain: cardamom-led LNDL; lipstick iris or Prada/Dior Homme drift; literal rose; sweet amber, vanilla, pastry, or cinnamon; leather, oud, smoke, tinctures, opoponax, or myrrh; Dihydromyrcenol sport-blue identity; Hedione or Iso E identity; hard amberwood walls; and multi-musk laundry effects.

