## Spatial, temporal, textural, transition, pressure/release, and recurrence maps

### Spatial planes

| Plane | Owners | Intended relationship |
|---|---|---|
| Front glint | Bergamot, lemon, aldehydes, pepper | Polish and cold cut disclose ginger rather than obscure it |
| Living middle | Ginger EO, Jessemal, Dihydrojasmone, Cis Jasmone, ionones | Warm tissue and violet cloth remain one subject |
| Rear contour | literal cedars, vetiver set, Koavone, Sandalore, Ebanol hypothesis | Dry grain and yielding interior oppose without forming an amberwood wall |
| Through-line / residue | Terpinyl Acetate, Coumarin, Tonka, Cashmeran, Benzyl Benzoate | Fiber, hay, textile, and quiet mass transform ginger into late residue |
| Aura | air field plus Romandolide | Negative space and one clean-woody musk outline the subject |

### Five temporal windows

| Window | Intended front | Intended middle | Intended rear / recurrence | Evidence state |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| opening, 0-5 min | polished rind, lemon, pepper, wet ginger | citral and terpene incision | first violet-metal and cedar glints | NOT TESTED |
| top, 5-30 min | ginger cortex contracts | Jessemal and jasmone expose warm fiber | leaf and metallic stitches sharpen the cloth | NOT TESTED |
| heart, 30-120 min | violet-green fiber | ionone and muguet cloth | cedar and vetiver become legible through bounded air | NOT TESTED |
| late heart, 2-6 h | dry violet-root line | tonka, coumarin, Sandalore, and Ebanol hypothesis yield inward | literal woods and Romandolide hold contour | NOT TESTED |
| drydown, 6-24 h | faint dry cut | hayed tonka and sandal warmth | cedar-vetiver residue inside one musk aura | NOT TESTED |

### Ten transition and recurrence links

| # | Link | Shared chemical or textural edge | Failure mode |
|---:|---|---|---|
| 1 | peel -> ginger cortex | citral, linalyl acetate, pepper, beta-pinene | citrus cleaner beside unrelated ginger |
| 2 | cortex -> rhizome heart | Ginger EO, Jessemal, Dihydrojasmone, Cis Jasmone | volatile ginger falls into a hollow middle |
| 3 | rhizome -> violet cloth | Cis Jasmone, retained floral tissue, ionones | violet appears as detached powder |
| 4 | cloth -> green incision | Leafovert, basil, Rose Oxide, Dynascone, Scentenal | tailored leaf perimeter disappears |
| 5 | green incision -> air | Cyclamen, Floralozone, Helional, bounded Hedione | green becomes flat, harsh, or marine |
| 6 | violet cloth -> cedar grain | Allyl Ionone, Dihydro Beta Ionone, Cashmeran, Iso E | cosmetic-to-wood splice |
| 7 | ginger fiber -> vetiver root | Terpinyl Acetate, clary, Koavone, Vetival | base loses the named subject |
| 8 | cedar grain -> yielding sandal | Koavone, Sandalore, bounded Ebanol hypothesis | woods become a rigid stack or creamy takeover |
| 9 | vetiver root -> tonka grain | Coumarin, Tonkarome, Tonka Absolute | tonka reads edible or pasted on |
| 10 | base interior -> aura | Ebanol hypothesis, Cashmeran, Romandolide | musk floats outside the perfume as detergent |

### Nineteen conserved textural roles

Polished; waxed; wet-cut; crisp; fatty; fibrous; tailored-cloth; leafy; metallic; bitter; humid; mineral; pencil-dry; rooty; hayed; creamy-yielding; textile; slow; clean-woody.

### Pressure, release, and recurrence

Ginger cut, bitter-green incision, literal dry grain, and mineral air provide pressure. Jasmone tissue, the violet cloth, bounded Hedione, Sandalore, the Ebanol hypothesis, and quiet matrix provide release. Late recurrence is relational rather than literal: terpinyl fiber, vetiver root, hayed tonka, cedar grain, and Romandolide recall ginger's dryness, warmth, and outline. None of these temporal or sensory effects has been observed.

