## Future mixing order

`FUTURE WORK / NO COMPOUNDING AUTHORIZED.` If physical work is later authorized: prepare and label all working stocks first; prepare the Ginger EO working stock from exactly 230 uL Ginger EO plus 660 uL DPG and reserve the complete 890 uL for one whole-stock addition; do not dose it by a rounded-percentage back-calculation; verify inventory identity and observed homogeneity under separate authority; combine quiet matrix and base rows, then cedar/vetiver and sandal/tonka rows, then violet/ginger tissue, then air/green traces, then volatile aperture; add the entire Ginger EO working stock once; add ethanol only after concentrate reconciliation; mature and inspect under a separately approved protocol. This route is NOT TESTED for homogeneity or stability. No mixing order is a safety, compatibility, or release clearance.

## Controlled blinded test plan

### Control qualification: Ebanol functional-approximation omission

- `A / EC+`: this V6 control, including Ebanol 30 uL and the complete 890 uL Ginger EO working stock made from 230 uL Ginger EO plus 660 uL DPG.
- `B / EC0`: omit Ebanol and instead prepare one separately labeled, whole-use B stock from 230 uL Ginger EO plus 690 uL DPG = 920 uL (`Ginger EO 25.000000% v/v in DPG — EC0`); this replaces A's combined 890 uL Ginger stock + 30 uL Ebanol block one-for-one. Every other row is identical. Nominal v/v arithmetic does not establish w/w equivalence, homogeneity, or stability.
- Both are raw-volume constant at 6,000 uL and 20% finished concentration. They are not active-mass constant because the exact question is whether the bounded Ebanol hypothesis adds useful yielding texture versus neutral carrier.
- Use at least two independently prepared master sets, duplicate coded pours, anonymous codes, AB/BA counterbalancing, equal application mass and substrate, separated sessions, and free description before scores.
- Read at 0, 5, 30, and 120 minutes, then 6 and 24 hours. Score L'Homme identity, ginger-to-violet continuity, cedar grain, yielding texture, creamy takeover, woody clutter, drydown pleasure, overall liking, re-smell desire, muddiness, harshness, and fatigue separately.
- Retain Ebanol in the family control only if both independent preparations show non-worse identity and liking plus a useful yielding transition without creamy/oriental drift. Null, discordant, or intensity-confounded outcomes remain `HOLD / NON-INFORMATIVE`.

### Secondary stock-gap diagnostics

Only after the Ebanol decision, test one axis at a time: bounded Hedione versus a carrier-matched omission in which the same complete 890 uL Ginger EO stock is retained and a separately labeled 200 uL DPG comparator aliquot replaces Hedione; then, if warranted, a current-owned leaf module versus matched carrier. Do not combine stock corrections in one causal claim. Later flankers compare against the qualified V6 control, never against historical V5 as if Polysantol were executable.

